WICImagingFactory::Instance() made a RefPtr from the plain pointer CoCreateInstance returned, which takes a reference
of its own: the one of CoCreateInstance was never released, a WIC factory lost per glyph surface (Cairo 1.18.6, which
creates the factory on every call). Commit 8c3a27e7 of the branch legacy of https://github.com/apotocki/cairo (commit
50f28511 of the branch d2d, which the option d2d builds).

diff --git a/src/win32/cairo-dwrite-font.cpp b/src/win32/cairo-dwrite-font.cpp
index ae3b01212..c44a241b1 100644
--- a/src/win32/cairo-dwrite-font.cpp
+++ b/src/win32/cairo-dwrite-font.cpp
@@ -187,7 +187,10 @@ public:
          */
         cairo_win32_ensure_mta ();
 
-        IWICImagingFactory *wic_factory;
+        /* CoCreateInstance gives the reference to the RefPtr: one made from
+         * a plain pointer would take another, never released.
+         */
+        RefPtr<IWICImagingFactory> wic_factory;
         hr = CoCreateInstance (CLSID_WICImagingFactory,
                                NULL,
                                CLSCTX_INPROC_SERVER,
